{:activity/_scope [{:activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193457} :activity/id #uuid "2acc7e09-91cc-5ff3-8a20-8051f891cc61" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193457 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193941 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to solve the following system of linear equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=1 \\\\ x-y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAs it stands, adding the two equations will not eliminate any of the variables. \n\nHowever, suppose we want to eliminate the variable $x$. We begin by multiplying the second equation by $\\color{blue}-1$, which gives the following equivalent system:\n\n![](images/72/724119f2404af61332fcabbb5cda3522f9d338a4c6427084e5901e1ca7cd4498.svg)\n\nThen, we add the two resulting equations together. This will eliminate the variable $x,$ allowing us to solve for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{x}+2y & =1 \\\\ -\\cancel{x}+y & =2 \\\\ (2y+y) & =(1+2) \\\\ 3y & =3 \\\\ y & =1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y=1.$ However, we still need to find $x.$ To do this, we substitute $y=1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}x-y & =-2 \\\\ x-(1) & =-2 \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-1$ and $y=1,$ which can be expressed as $(-1, 1).$" :tutorial/id #uuid "97211668-1a0d-5471-9a0a-c223dfb2f8a6" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8703 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "6912b472-9f6a-508c-a69c-38d65838fd66" :step/math-academy-id 196622 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193458}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193458 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192654 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192585 :question/id #uuid "c700cc22-203a-5ad3-913c-e5eb507e22e3" :question/math-academy-id "e-13995" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}a+4b &=1 \\\\ 2a+b &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $a$ from this system by filling in the missing information below.\n\n$\\qquad$ *To eliminate $a,$ multiply the $\\,\\textbf{__________}\\,$equation by $\\,\\textbf{______}\\,$, \nand add the equations.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $a$ in the first equation is $1,$ while in the second equation it is $2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-2},$ then the coefficient of $a$ will turn into $-2,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $2$ in the second equation.\n\n![](images/2b/2b0aa0d1dbfeb1e711bde6e7741fe5706aa126d71c44ae417d3c78d01b83547a.svg)\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $a$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{-2a}-8b & =-2 \\\\ \\cancel{2a}+b & =-5 \\\\ (-8b+b) & =(-2-5) \\\\ -7b & =-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*To eliminate $a,$ multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-2},$ and add the equations*."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93dcc73c-ce2d-5fa3-b32b-9fc600fb269e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049060}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509241 :question-generator/id #uuid "b0954483-dbae-52d5-aa27-0d7a9746e93c" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186192654.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193241 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e0b7d00-1654-52b7-9052-7a91aba67a61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191238} {:answer/id #uuid "8f6b863b-f16e-552b-a6e4-05539ba27cdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191239} {:answer/id #uuid "11e4d5ce-3fc3-53e8-8584-1042acdeff24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191240} {:answer/id #uuid "41f6c130-1233-542f-a28b-1ce8647c5922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191241}] :answer-field/id #uuid "379e8fcc-29be-5846-9a9e-189e462ab1f1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191237} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15818fb1-87d0-562d-b98a-b5e28f06c22d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191243} {:answer/id #uuid "191da071-188e-5707-938f-7f3a2b084c8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191244}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3bd31a5e-f325-573b-965a-e81ee45bc294" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191242}] :question/id #uuid "1d7ff6e0-7f69-5f77-a026-49d6c5918b17" :question/math-academy-id "q-210858" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n${x - y = 1; - 7x + 5y = 9$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $x$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $x$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a45b4e3-546f-58ce-bc86-f21f14be794d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191246} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce11990-8f77-5ca3-bb7c-924e6d9f7e71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191247}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186191246} :answer-field/id #uuid "f741ca69-46ce-51d3-89ee-ebd3b9b5298e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2d6ae65-382f-5725-8d12-368b3161c220" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191249} {:answer/id #uuid "e5dd37b2-c127-522c-8a0a-7efbd395282d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191250} {:answer/id #uuid "2d811e29-d735-5f20-b57d-488fa19f4d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191251} {:answer/id #uuid "43aa771d-f31e-507f-a36a-818c77be68a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191252}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186191250} :answer-field/id #uuid "da2c168a-6d3a-5018-b549-be3fcba5455b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191248}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "35ea5fbe-0a0e-53a6-8872-3cafe1bfb9c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-210859" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3s+4t &=8 \\\\ s+5t &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $s$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $s,$ multiply the \n{{field-1}} \nequation by \n{{field-2}}, \nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $3,$ while in the second equation it is $1.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-3,$ then the coefficient of $s$ will turn into $-3,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $3$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3s+4t &=8 \\\\ (\\,s+5t &=10\\,)\\,\\times (-3)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3s+4t &=8 \\\\ -3s-15t &=-30\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{3s}+4t & =8 \\\\ -\\cancel{3s}-15t & =-30 \\\\ (4t-15t) & =(8-30) \\\\ -11t & =-22 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*Multiply the $\\text{second}$ equation by $-3,$ and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508917 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "396c0c6a-1e03-5316-868c-3693041a6a8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508474} {:answer/id #uuid "7405e912-7fbf-5e14-9ed1-9fa8aad46b93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508557}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508474} :answer-field/id #uuid "15d7b3eb-155c-54a4-84ac-4a02f7b9e7e6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508817} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "564482bf-2dea-55bc-82ec-61c16390e434" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508516} {:answer/id #uuid "802cf47d-d04d-59cb-9afb-86ba6294bc49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508578} {:answer/id #uuid "82dc65ea-5abd-5f0e-b1d6-8d53cd015c74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508583} {:answer/id #uuid "ed089b80-c77d-5a59-8fbf-99ba45caaf88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508769}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508516} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fa84268-830c-548e-ba16-e867f14c3bf3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2a68ca7c-dc16-5d70-b5c4-e7c98a96c8e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-238035" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}10x-3y &=36 \\\\ 2x+5y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $x$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $x,$ multiply the \n{{field-1}} \nequation by \n{{field-2}}, \nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $10,$ while in the second equation it is $2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-5,$ then the coefficient of $x$ will turn into $-10,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $10$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}10x-3y &=36 \\\\ (\\,2x+5y &=-4\\,)\\,\\times (-5)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}10x-3y &=36 \\\\ -10x-25y &=20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{10x}-3y & =36 \\\\ -\\cancel{10x}-25y & =20 \\\\ (-3y-25y) & =(36+20) \\\\ -28y & =56 \\\\ y & =-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*Multiply the $\\text{second}$ equation by $-5,$ and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509133 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53ecbda6-7a57-5ced-b37b-67f3e0611d56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509157} {:answer/id #uuid "5de6e3ad-5e74-5eaf-9366-87ca894f9566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509165} {:answer/id #uuid "653a3e3d-63fb-5473-b192-2fbab82ed7c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509171} {:answer/id #uuid "b9ab6b5e-f7d5-5ac1-8e90-66c8945a033a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509206}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509157} :answer-field/id #uuid "55b88cc5-050d-5ed4-9161-b5ccd94b7ecc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71254510-dc0b-5ac5-8725-9ee4cc50d177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509180} {:answer/id #uuid "73f72834-ef24-5b1d-976b-7feaf1a9d939" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509181}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509181} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff3ef9d4-e8b8-5b98-a4cf-98c00e7da24b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "19893126-a14f-5669-bf14-122fe45ed903" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-2s - 5t = -4; s - t = 7$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $s$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $s$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $-2$, while in the second equation it is $1$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}2}$, then the coefficient of $s$ will turn into $2$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-2$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-2s - 5t = -4; (s - t = 7)\\cdot (2)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2s - 5t &= -4 \\\\\n2s - 2t &= 14 \\\\\n(-5t - 2t) &= (-4 + 14) \\\\\n-7t &= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $s$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509137 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aeebf26-5c1d-5f04-804f-fdbb0e881867" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509125} {:answer/id #uuid "293070fd-4043-5661-98e9-7be503a082d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509142} {:answer/id #uuid "692cee72-bfa9-5fd6-abba-b11a7a8be386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509174} {:answer/id #uuid "dd6cd90f-5e7f-57b0-8d7c-57a397aef73b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509217}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509217} :answer-field/id #uuid "284ec41e-07e8-5e62-9a65-b25ff0d33732" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509141} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b5300f7-a4f7-59ac-a98c-94a32ace5760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509175} {:answer/id #uuid "eb358494-ea2b-5da8-af38-6fcccefe9b82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509223}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509223} :answer-field/id #uuid "b87d9f3f-8596-5816-b8ed-4b34e42d4362" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1b8974fc-30d6-5417-a48d-1b3409dc7e93" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{18s + 3t = 3; 3s - t = -1$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $s$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $s$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $18$, while in the second equation it is $3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}-6}$, then the coefficient of $s$ will turn into $-18$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $18$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{18s + 3t = 3; (3s - t = -1)\\cdot (-6)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n18s + 3t &= 3 \\\\\n-18s + 6t &= 6 \\\\\n(3t + 6t) &= (3 + 6) \\\\\n9t &= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $s$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-6}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509162 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d30a9310-132f-58dd-adc9-7ca05291ae85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509211} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd64ef7-1c64-574c-8ea8-0d518b6c5c9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509236}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509211} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2fe93e8-fd8c-56bd-b346-a7ee96a13287" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509219} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b91c01f-0cc8-50d2-a732-4c140bdaf327" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509138} {:answer/id #uuid "1e35d57f-3afd-5872-ad5d-ee2f75273b1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509139} {:answer/id #uuid "375829a1-3779-5a18-8d44-baa3aa8fdefe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509145} {:answer/id #uuid "faed50d6-cd2f-55aa-979a-48cbb4f4b48d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509234}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509138} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffee62a7-4adb-5d89-b9c0-c0c82f2fbecb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5c3fcbc5-6f71-51a3-bc0e-dcb789c48f3d" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{4x - y = 7; -2x - 2y = -6$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $x$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $x$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $4$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}2}$, then the coefficient of $x$ will turn into $-4$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{4x - y = 7; (-2x - 2y = -6)\\cdot (2)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - y &= 7 \\\\\n-4x - 4y &= -12 \\\\\n(-y - 4y) &= (7 - 12) \\\\\n-5y &= -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $x$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509164 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77ee12f8-d1f3-570d-a553-36dadb480f02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509183} {:answer/id #uuid "a65b148e-ebaa-5313-b824-fd0cb34f8f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509200}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509183} :answer-field/id #uuid "89a51c62-b05a-540b-9e93-1b6230dda76a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509189} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5fd99a4-ddcf-55d1-9b15-5ac5dff61a43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509204} {:answer/id #uuid "d687931e-a29d-5efd-b673-e9deab3adf2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509215} {:answer/id #uuid "f4498730-43c5-503f-8dfb-ad2ab3b897e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509230} {:answer/id #uuid "f6ea7f1e-f6a3-55e0-89b8-23a9a14cd4a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509232}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509232} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcd64ba7-5484-592a-b858-d730e378e03f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509235}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5d211815-c8ae-5268-9f21-aa7a3a361a49" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{s + 5t = 8; -6s - 3t = -11$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $s$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $s$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $1$, while in the second equation it is $-6$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}6}$, then the coefficient of $s$ will turn into $6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-6$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(s + 5t = 8)\\cdot (6); -6s - 3t = -11\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6s + 30t &= 48 \\\\\n-6s - 3t &= -11 \\\\\n(30t - 3t) &= (48 - 11) \\\\\n27t &= 37\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $s$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}6}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509176 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b6c98e2-b881-582d-9f5f-0b5e631af0d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509136} {:answer/id #uuid "41817a51-4551-5887-8edc-4f68222f6c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509154}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509154} :answer-field/id #uuid "1017d759-4b65-5a74-84cd-294669705e4d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509129} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9355d920-8afb-5d5c-bf18-878687504ae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509194} {:answer/id #uuid "a71c0001-ba06-517a-9199-dabed82358f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509201} {:answer/id #uuid "def5b0ef-7a2c-5d73-a7df-a22cf11be967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509218} {:answer/id #uuid "ec9fe144-6fa4-557e-8a92-e87377d7bdec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509226}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509226} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd5d39b8-c2f4-51d5-b867-81477e252946" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6cb94d02-a970-59bb-bbf4-9561546e5e3d" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-u + 7v = 0; 5u + 6v = -3$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $u$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $u$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $u$ in the first equation is $-1$, while in the second equation it is $5$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}5}$, then the coefficient of $u$ will turn into $-5$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $5$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-u + 7v = 0)\\cdot (5); 5u + 6v = -3\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $u$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5u + 35v &= 0 \\\\\n5u + 6v &= -3 \\\\\n(35v + 6v) &= (0 - 3) \\\\\n41v &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $u$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}5}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38a5e8cf-9679-5e37-af4f-2b17615357b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509148} {:answer/id #uuid "5f107f49-ca98-5c5c-ba01-7ed409d9584c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509167} {:answer/id #uuid "cab95ace-4eda-5db9-84f4-6e8b591ffd8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509209} {:answer/id #uuid "f64438e6-d808-5371-8b19-8ad9d9da997a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509231}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509209} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a877f6f-f677-54d3-8e13-f1e41a168341" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509196} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5508c343-1cde-52e2-b519-45724995255d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509158} {:answer/id #uuid "634fb5d2-df05-5b0b-b07f-054996dc4e91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509169}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509158} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8160bd8-72f0-543f-a4bb-48e47b164659" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7a39a169-0a8a-5634-a2bd-69230a2e80b3" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-x + 6y = -10; 3x - 6y = -10$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $x$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $x$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $-1$, while in the second equation it is $3$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}3}$, then the coefficient of $x$ will turn into $-3$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $3$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-x + 6y = -10)\\cdot (3); 3x - 6y = -10\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x + 18y &= -30 \\\\\n3x - 6y &= -10 \\\\\n(18y - 6y) &= (-30 - 10) \\\\\n12y &= -40\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $x$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}3}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509190 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c7580cd-b447-5b07-8244-aa60ed8b432b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509127} {:answer/id #uuid "37f6dc11-926d-5c03-9805-d02d2532713f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509146}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509127} :answer-field/id #uuid "38297468-7ab5-5b91-8e12-ca8efeca13e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509147} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aec4d68-692c-572d-ac3c-b01bfca6be6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509135} {:answer/id #uuid "91e3d394-d205-5608-b462-7568316fcc28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509193} {:answer/id #uuid "d4fbe5d2-a01c-5b88-b8b7-675b4ad0be31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509213} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d2b2ff-1278-5e85-9a71-91debd3eb472" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509227}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509213} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f99a074-f636-5d4f-ba30-33d540aa5e50" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8c460209-35ec-5be6-8f7c-2d8bae28aa03" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{15u - 6v = -10; 3u - 8v = -12$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $u$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $u$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $u$ in the first equation is $15$, while in the second equation it is $3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}-5}$, then the coefficient of $u$ will turn into $-15$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $15$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{15u - 6v = -10; (3u - 8v = -12)\\cdot (-5)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $u$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n15u - 6v &= -10 \\\\\n-15u + 40v &= 60 \\\\\n(-6v + 40v) &= (-10 + 60) \\\\\n34v &= 50\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $u$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-5}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f820aee-0719-5afc-b3d3-14f46271246a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509128} {:answer/id #uuid "cbac78f7-7dff-51a3-a55d-073dd5230aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509210}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509128} :answ