u$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}5}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509233 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04628238-d380-592d-b5b6-3c682a225f46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509124} {:answer/id #uuid "a87f090a-c78c-5737-88f2-7b5e3dfd3525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509202}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509202} :answer-field/id #uuid "8250c2eb-d7f6-5ac0-a534-35ae93df8f7e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509187} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bb4b0b3-7585-53b9-9698-315b218cf567" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509126} {:answer/id #uuid "3452e2e9-29bb-5de6-ac26-87db98641b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509144} {:answer/id #uuid "3d80b461-5f25-562b-8ac3-2849bd730f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509152} {:answer/id #uuid "56465b81-892c-5a5e-a9e1-a8f703c83857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509160}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509144} :answer-field/id #uuid "db26b532-577a-58da-91ab-fcfc6b38cd25" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f78c7c38-9036-5285-9151-a9dd571f995d" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{20u + 9v = 7; 4u - 8v = -12$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $u$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $u$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $u$ in the first equation is $20$, while in the second equation it is $4$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}-5}$, then the coefficient of $u$ will turn into $-20$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $20$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{20u + 9v = 7; (4u - 8v = -12)\\cdot (-5)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $u$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n20u + 9v &= 7 \\\\\n-20u + 40v &= 60 \\\\\n(9v + 40v) &= (7 + 60) \\\\\n49v &= 67\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $u$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-5}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39984c68-52c5-5346-96ed-793bff46e6f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509150} {:answer/id #uuid "4713ec37-422e-594c-819d-cacd1edf2a8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509155}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509155} :answer-field/id #uuid "751b0f60-f8d4-5160-8cc1-482c0b17d4f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c0c0b8-da16-5447-87d9-10a1ded8b80f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509130} {:answer/id #uuid "17edb0af-3a94-5780-a31a-1fbd748bfaea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509131} {:answer/id #uuid "7957b3a2-96f1-51ce-9c08-33f9ec62fbb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509184} {:answer/id #uuid "a5dfa42e-5ab0-5456-b0d7-5b7718419449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509199}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509184} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ae02db1-b940-5eef-9978-b83d1e237256" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fdbe5bab-0875-5446-89a1-bb1bcb354802" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{3u + 6v = 3; -u + 5v = 8$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $u$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $u$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $u$ in the first equation is $3$, while in the second equation it is $-1$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}3}$, then the coefficient of $u$ will turn into $-3$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $3$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{3u + 6v = 3; (-u + 5v = 8)\\cdot (3)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $u$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3u + 6v &= 3 \\\\\n-3u + 15v &= 24 \\\\\n(6v + 15v) &= (3 + 24) \\\\\n21v &= 27\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $u$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}3}$, and add the equations*."}] :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable"} :step/id #uuid "49980fef-ad30-5576-b1f1-83af40688b8d" :step/math-academy-id 196623 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193459}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193459 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192586 :question/id #uuid "eb7f1f32-1a5c-526e-878b-8046c4feb8c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-13997" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+4y &=2 \\\\ x-2y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $y$ from this system by filling in the missing information below.\n\n$\\qquad$ *To eliminate $y,$ multiply the $\\,\\textbf{__________}\\,$equation by $\\,\\textbf{______}\\,$, \nand add the equations.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $4,$ while in the second equation it is $-2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}2},$ then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $-4,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the first equation.\n\n![](images/0e/0e494f68d4859d46c3c369274e415f10a850c664343d41cce8dcfcfdd660e17c.svg)\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+\\cancel{4y} & =2 \\\\ 2x-\\cancel{4y} & =8 \\\\ (3x+2x) & =(2+8) \\\\ 5x & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*To eliminate $y,$ multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2},$ and add the equations*."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508377 :question-generator/id #uuid "835d8836-7a8d-5bd9-ad81-8fb2ebfafdee" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186192655.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805f8ad6-7fae-5b23-9e8d-6ae094055dbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191254} {:answer/id #uuid "90021633-7a04-57cc-a6b7-c9aa58120746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191255} {:answer/id #uuid "ba18e7d3-a103-5f29-b2f2-a9cc52a7d7c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191256} {:answer/id #uuid "48b2983a-4a87-59af-9b24-bfd7e5742c7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :