 -6 \\\\\n(-30a + 8a) &= (-36 - 6) \\\\\n-22a &= -42\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-6}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "621daa3f-f6bd-5b36-9874-b650477f8088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508305} {:answer/id #uuid "a2985571-dbf8-51bf-a4f9-d9b6a23fb056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508332} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e22db4-43ce-578a-b7fc-4204d456f11a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508343} {:answer/id #uuid "ef083660-ccf2-5acb-becc-021580a075e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508368}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508343} :answer-field/id #uuid "68ee5b4f-0b69-590f-a728-db8f8c5b2a77" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508308} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5eb82832-5ab9-55eb-b044-1486415663e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508302} {:answer/id #uuid "95d49c0e-b75e-5cf5-9189-284664b8174c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508326}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508326} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b6a41f-baa5-5e85-8063-37cfcdc79ce1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "574b99c3-fa99-567e-a234-991332375ffc" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-8a + b = 5; -2a - 6b = 5$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $1$, while in the second equation it is $-6$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}6}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-6$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-8a + b = 5)\\cdot (6); -2a - 6b = 5\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-48a + 6b &= 30 \\\\\n-2a - 6b &= 5 \\\\\n(-48a - 2a) &= (30 + 5) \\\\\n-50a &= 35\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}6}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508307 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04417b27-9946-5125-9466-90e0f7a986c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508243} {:answer/id #uuid "3e2838d9-13e8-537e-97ea-602c03007640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508279}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508243} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d9ddd9b-417d-5c44-844c-4b4a797676c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508270} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19fa65bd-e0ac-53c5-ad03-2a4fda5a68fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508259} {:answer/id #uuid "52fa9519-a033-5b42-9165-65290877079d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508293} {:answer/id #uuid "616b773c-eb7f-53d8-8033-ae2212b1eda3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508304} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2e6827-1e74-5d70-9818-fa1b3f6a26d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508317}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508304} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd1e4eda-122a-5639-8952-d1178bcfef7b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6780c205-51e6-5535-82c2-0fc482ef81fb" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$\\{a - 3b = -6; -7a - 15b = 9$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-3$, while in the second equation it is $-15$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-5}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $15$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-15$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(a - 3b = -6)\\cdot (-5); -7a - 15b = 9\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5a + 15b &= 30 \\\\\n-7a - 15b &= 9 \\\\\n(-5a - 7a) &= (30 + 9) \\\\\n-12a &= 39\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-5}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508321 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33534e52-22a6-53b6-ab24-f2fc95901ef6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508273} {:answer/id #uuid "7d632778-d7d0-5b8e-8054-b8393a63d67d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508316} {:answer/id #uuid "bac5aab2-c0b2-503d-8b54-7be5dbbb5e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508340} {:answer/id #uuid "f826503c-35ad-5dec-94b5-1a3ecf16f589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508372}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508340} :answer-field/id #uuid "03b806d6-996d-59c5-bbcd-324cbd1e9495" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508242} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f2c2bcf-334b-56b0-a302-17ebf4f4cff4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508251} {:answer/id #uuid "53b071d1-754c-5b35-a614-05465b4639f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508294}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508294} :answer-field/id #uuid "760e3944-245b-5965-ab85-16e5a3fc8a38" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "88d9972c-3f5b-5e57-9021-7026fbb79903" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$\\{10a + 3b = -1; 9a + 18b = -5$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $3$, while in the second equation it is $18$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-6}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $-18$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $18$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(10a + 3b = -1)\\cdot (-6); 9a + 18b = -5\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-60a - 18b &= 6 \\\\\n9a + 18b &= -5 \\\\\n(-60a + 9a) &= (6 - 5) \\\\\n-51a &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-6}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508322 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e1e4729-9ebb-50b7-97a6-6a0b8db4e6d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508311} {:answer/id #uuid "b459b991-eaa4-553b-9c8a-0dd1e8acb702" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508339}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508311} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf884d6e-dce2-519f-ab28-c6007c78d5de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508341} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27a58455-667c-5f6b-8469-30df6a8a1ac8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508265} {:answer/id #uuid "36b3ff1d-16cc-5ec1-8363-7931928f70f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508275} {:answer/id #uuid "7591a0ea-d50c-56c3-b207-4eacbbc2fd2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508314} {:answer/id #uuid "9f13ab07-f7ad-59d3-b0e2-6a9789ab2b74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508330}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508275} :answer-field/id #uuid "f90f8a44-dc14-58ae-923e-fe1760ae1c20" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "89017559-2077-57e8-85e1-d0eabb36b51a" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-3x - y = 5; -8x - 2y = 3$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $y$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $y$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $-1$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-2}$, then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $2$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-2$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-3x - y = 5)\\cdot (-2); -8x - 2y = 3\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x + 2y &= -10 \\\\\n-8x - 2y &= 3 \\\\\n(6x - 8x) &= (-10 + 3) \\\\\n-2x &= -7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $y$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-2}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1492c2d9-3b96-5d99-af2f-6e353ea4288a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508256} {:answer/id #uuid "3c58fb78-1c5a-5c15-a174-22de3ccedad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508277} {:answer/id #uuid "41e49d7e-68bc-5ebc-a9ef-96bd0d52383e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508281} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4f2e04-8657-5d5c-84fc-fa0044c746d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508375}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508281} :answer-field/id #uuid "6286a964-ba5c-565d-8d4e-a9e48c8480d3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answe