$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $15$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-15$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-5a - 15b = 8; (-8a - 3b = 10)\\cdot (-5)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5a - 15b &= 8 \\\\\n40a + 15b &= -50 \\\\\n(-5a + 40a) &= (8 - 50) \\\\\n35a &= -42\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-5}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508342 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "220d1f0d-705a-51be-82e7-454a15c207cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508263} {:answer/id #uuid "46b40b50-8f41-5621-8507-c13a24eb8d3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508284} {:answer/id #uuid "9de0642e-8140-505e-bfef-fd699ee965c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508329} {:answer/id #uuid "e0cb89cc-3ada-54c1-844b-f8a94e1b7b32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508358}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508263} :answer-field/id #uuid "0498b1cf-1084-5733-bdf4-ea8c3243f834" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508244} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd114504-60b2-56a9-b45f-e2f46590bd88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508351} {:answer/id #uuid "ec7df554-c07e-5acc-aefd-f039f9b1770d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508367}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508367} :answer-field/id #uuid "40ecc8a2-2592-5ad6-9e81-bebf58162924" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c27baa0c-b46f-57bf-b6fc-d115fa72a94d" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$\\{10a + 3b = -1; 9a + 9b = -5$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $3$, while in the second equation it is $9$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-3}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $-9$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $9$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(10a + 3b = -1)\\cdot (-3); 9a + 9b = -5\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-30a - 9b &= 3 \\\\\n9a + 9b &= -5 \\\\\n(-30a + 9a) &= (3 - 5) \\\\\n-21a &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-3}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508345 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19abff8d-ae9e-5607-a20e-fabfdd36db34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508258} {:answer/id #uuid "20a941f3-cb0b-5f69-ab43-56c13080d620" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508261} {:answer/id #uuid "46814826-f010-593a-b3e8-5f63f785645f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508282} {:answer/id #uuid "5594cdc5-034f-5627-abd8-dfbefb4c1912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218650