 #uuid "29b35e16-f22f-597d-93ba-b82e8bf204f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508267} {:answer/id #uuid "e49c439c-a969-56e3-a863-ca3dbe265312" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508363}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508363} :answer-field/id #uuid "f300ef54-4bdd-5f40-99eb-20c59ef401be" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0b561ffa-2e48-5300-9c0f-dc37e617a67e" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-8a + 4b = 5; -2a - 12b = 5$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $4$, while in the second equation it is $-12$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}3}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $12$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-12$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-8a + 4b = 5)\\cdot (3); -2a - 12b = 5\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-24a + 12b &= 15 \\\\\n-2a - 12b &= 5 \\\\\n(-24a - 2a) &= (15 + 5) \\\\\n-26a &= 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}3}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508268 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f8e738-0572-5121-922d-d8e38fb86c3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508286} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd845b8-5401-5d60-a03b-9a759c275fb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508287} {:answer/id #uuid "a112c9cb-8d88-5623-a13e-d989a8243fa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508331} {:answer/id #uuid "f803e108-8054-582f-a2d5-145329d8c27d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508371}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508286} :answer-field/id #uuid "075b0439-b453-57c0-a744-1bcb64243346" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508247} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c454440-b1b8-513b-9f73-0f7dc8536063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508328} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e83d65-e084-55b9-9c2a-92d5a80729d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508334}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508328} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccc2f91f-fe2d-582d-b3e5-fdf6e12b119f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2b1cb458-ef47-59b8-b185-bca727e5bdc2" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{5a - 4b = 6; 8a - 24b = -6$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-4$, while in the second equation it is $-24$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-6}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $24$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-24$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(5a - 4b = 6)\\cdot (-6); 8a - 24b = -6\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-30a + 24b &= -36 \\\\\n8a - 24b &= -6 \\\\\n(-30a + 8a) &= (-36 - 6) \\\\\n-22a &= -42\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-6}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "621daa3f-f6bd-5b36-9874-b650477f8088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508305} {:answer/id #uuid "a2985571-dbf8-51bf-a4f9-d9b6a23fb056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508332} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e22db4-43ce-578a-b7fc-4204d456f11a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508343} {:answer/id #uuid "ef083660-ccf2-5acb-becc-021580a075e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508368}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508343} :answer-field/id #uuid "68ee5b4f-0b69-590f-a728-db8f8c5b2a77" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508308} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5eb82832-5ab9-55eb-b044-1486415663e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508302} {:answer/id #uuid "95d49c0e-b75e-5cf5-9189-284664b8174c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508326}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508326} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b6a41f-baa5-5e85-8063-37cfcdc79ce1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "574b99c3-fa99-567e-a234-991332375ffc" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-8a + b = 5; -2a - 6b = 5$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $1$, while in the second equation it is $-6$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}6}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-6$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-8a + b = 5)\\cdot (6); -2a - 6b = 5\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-48a + 6b &= 30 \\\\\n-2a - 6b &= 5 \\\\\n(-48a - 2a) &= (30 + 5) \\\\\n-50a &= 35\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}6}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508307 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04417b27-9946-5125-9466-90e0f7a986c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508243} {:answer/id #uuid "3e2838d9-13e8-537e-97ea-602c03007640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508279}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508243} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d9ddd9b-417d-5c44-844c-4b4a797676c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508270} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19fa65bd-e0ac-53c5-ad03-2a4fda5a68fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508259} {:answer/id #uuid "52fa9519-a033-5b42-9165-65290877079d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508293} {:answer/id #uuid "616b773c-eb7f-53d8-8033-ae2212b1eda3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508304} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2e6827-1e74-5d70-9818-fa1b3f6a26d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508317}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508304} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd1e4eda-122a-5639-8952-d1178bcfef7b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6780c205-51e6-5535-82c2-0fc482ef81fb" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$\\{a - 3b = -6; -7a - 15b = 9$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-3$, while in the second equation it is $-15$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-5}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $15$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-15$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(a - 3b = -6)\\cdot (-5); -7a - 15b = 9\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5a + 15b &= 30 \\\\\n-7a - 15b &= 9 \\\\\n(-5a - 7a) &= (30 + 9) \\\\\n-12a &= 39\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-5}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508321 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33534e52-22a6-53b6-ab24-f2fc95901ef6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508273} {:answer/id #uuid "7d632778-d7d0-5b8e-8054-b8393a63d67d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508316} {:answer/id #uuid "bac5aab2-c0b2-503d-8b54-7be5dbbb5e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508340} {:answer/id #uuid "f826503c-35ad-5dec-94b5-1a3ecf16f589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508372}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508340} :answer-field/id #uuid "03b806d6-996d-59c5-bbcd-324cbd1e9495" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508242} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f2c2bcf-334b-56b0-a302-17ebf4f4cff4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508251} {:answer/id #uuid "53b071d1-754c-5b35-a614-05465b4639f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508294}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508294} :answer-field/id #uuid "760e3944-245b-5965-ab85-16e5a3fc8a38" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "88d9972c-3f5b-5e57-9021-7026fbb79903" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$\\{10a + 3b = -1; 9a + 18b = -5$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $3$, while in the second equation it is $18$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-6}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $-18$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $18$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(10a + 3b = -1)\\cdot (-6); 9a + 18b = -5\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-60a - 18b &= 6 \\\\\n9a + 18b &= -5 \\\\\n(-60a + 9a) &= (6 - 5) \\\\\n-51a &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-6}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508322 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e1e4729-9ebb-50b7-97a6-6a0b8db4e6d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508311} {:answer/id #uuid "b459b991-eaa4-553b-9c8a-0dd1e8acb702" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508339}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508311} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf884d6e-dce2-519f-ab28-c6007c78d5de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508341} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27a58455-667c-5f6b-8469-30df6a8a1ac8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508265} {:answer/id #uuid "36b3ff1d-16cc-5ec1-8363-7931928f70f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508275} {:answer/id #uuid "7591a0ea-d50c-56c3-b207-4eacbbc2fd2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508314} {:answer/id #uuid "9f13ab07-f7ad-59d3-b0e2-6a9789ab2b74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508330}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508275} :answer-field/id #uuid "f90f8a44-dc14-58ae-923e-fe1760ae1c20" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "89017559-2077-57e8-85e1-d0eabb36b51a" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-3x - y = 5; -8x - 2y = 3$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $y$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $y$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $-1$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-2}$, then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $2$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-2$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-3x - y = 5)\\cdot (-2); -8x - 2y = 3\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x + 2y &= -10 \\\\\n-8x - 2y &= 3 \\\\\n(6x - 8x) &= (-10 + 3) \\\\\n-2x &= -7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $y$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-2}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1492c2d9-3b96-5d99-af2f-6e353ea4288a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508256} {:answer/id #uuid "3c58fb78-1c5a-5c15-a174-22de3ccedad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508277} {:answer/id #uuid "41e49d7e-68bc-5ebc-a9ef-96bd0d52383e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508281} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4f2e04-8657-5d5c-84fc-fa0044c746d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508375}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508281} :answer-field/id #uuid "6286a964-ba5c-565d-8d4e-a9e48c8480d3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508306} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f61eeb6-cc93-5c08-b75c-f89886ef7e12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508252} {:answer/id #uuid "4f59c118-e786-5d13-acd5-e63e1183ebe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508290}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508290} :answer-field/id #uuid "e42b3517-335b-54fb-8f83-1c9cab494239" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "997e6dc4-14e3-5976-b4b9-16bbe485f4b0" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-3x - 2y = 5; -8x - 4y = 3$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $y$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $y$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $-2$, while in the second equation it is $-4$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-2}$, then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $4$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-4$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-3x - 2y = 5)\\cdot (-2); -8x - 4y = 3\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x + 4y &= -10 \\\\\n-8x - 4y &= 3 \\\\\n(6x - 8x) &= (-10 + 3) \\\\\n-2x &= -7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $y$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-2}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508333 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11e65d3b-c190-5cd9-8a2d-a34b04008864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508254} {:answer/id #uuid "a7cfa321-7684-5b8e-9a83-5671a3ae619b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508336}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508254} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cf2b31d-6044-5372-9c5a-c69f14f283df" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508310} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f2ef0e2-c929-5d5d-acd3-2bf9f6dee047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508289} {:answer/id #uuid "58d2767f-c4de-5274-b3c9-0c73323041ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508300} {:answer/id #uuid "86ac76c8-afa9-53b8-b8a4-1797ce46604a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508319} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f7ae80-61c0-5732-91e8-7d4017bd7623" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508359}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508319} :answer-field/id #uuid "74be7076-138c-597e-b8be-bd971a1c8b20" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a2bc7b54-6c53-543f-b23a-786a9000e0b8" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-5a - 15b = 8; -8a - 3b = 10$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-15$, while in the second equation it is $-3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}-5}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $15$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-15$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-5a - 15b = 8; (-8a - 3b = 10)\\cdot (-5)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5a - 15b &= 8 \\\\\n40a + 15b &= -50 \\\\\n(-5a + 40a) &= (8 - 50) \\\\\n35a &= -42\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-5}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508342 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "220d1f0d-705a-51be-82e7-454a15c207cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508263} {:answer/id #uuid "46b40b50-8f41-5621-8507-c13a24eb8d3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508284} {:answer/id #uuid "9de0642e-8140-505e-bfef-fd699ee965c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508329} {:answer/id #uuid "e0cb89cc-3ada-54c1-844b-f8a94e1b7b32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508358}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508263} :answer-field/id #uuid "0498b1cf-1084-5733-bdf4-ea8c3243f834" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508244} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd114504-60b2-56a9-b45f-e2f46590bd88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508351} {:answer/id #uuid "ec7df554-c07e-5acc-aefd-f039f9b1770d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508367}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508367} :answer-field/id #uuid "40ecc8a2-2592-5ad6-9e81-bebf58162924" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c27baa0c-b46f-57bf-b6fc-d115fa72a94d" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$\\{10a + 3b = -1; 9a + 9b = -5$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $3$, while in the second equation it is $9$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-3}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $-9$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $9$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(10a + 3b = -1)\\cdot (-3); 9a + 9b = -5\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-30a - 9b &= 3 \\\\\n9a + 9b &= -5 \\\\\n(-30a + 9a) &= (3 - 5) \\\\\n-21a &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-3}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508345 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19abff8d-ae9e-5607-a20e-fabfdd36db34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508258} {:answer/id #uuid "20a941f3-cb0b-5f69-ab43-56c13080d620" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508261} {:answer/id #uuid "46814826-f010-593a-b3e8-5f63f785645f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508282} {:answer/id #uuid "5594cdc5-034f-5627-abd8-dfbefb4c1912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508296}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508282} :answer-field/id #uuid "4818456c-7db3-59a9-b5db-3d94bdb07372" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508285} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50462789-9e2f-5032-b20b-8a96a67c5b5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508291} {:answer/id #uuid "ca8962f5-867a-5f1f-8e7a-03e4ad907c94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508348}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508348} :answer-field/id #uuid "e53c9495-4b32-5a29-a292-0a16103e681d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c7e5405c-436e-5c7d-914e-306e64abbe5d" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-8a + 4b = 5; -2a - 24b = 5$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $4$, while in the second equation it is $-24$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}6}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $24$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-24$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-8a + 4b = 5)\\cdot (6); -2a - 24b = 5\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-48a + 24b &= 30 \\\\\n-2a - 24b &= 5 \\\\\n(-48a - 2a) &= (30 + 5) \\\\\n-50a &= 35\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}6}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508349 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3329bb61-ee30-5582-b95e-93e49d25acbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508272} {:answer/id #uuid "5745dbcd-d2ec-538d-a5c0-6e40a55ff9c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508297}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508297} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b6e85c3-b039-528d-a630-269f4ab66bb7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508309} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7589e36d-b3bd-5962-bc29-ef4192f475f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508313} {:answer/id #uuid "c7eecde5-9335-5d7e-894a-906a63b21f24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508346} {:answer/id #uuid "c93a3f98-da46-5359-80b0-24e43b80b96b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508347} {:answer/id #uuid "d016ec66-1262-59a6-a15b-893c32493375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508352}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508313} :answer-field/id #uuid "873c2de2-15f7-503c-a9ac-a78b7c9793bb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508320}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cbd0b334-3f69-5bfe-96e0-237eb18aaf58" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$\\{a - b = -6; -7a - 3b = 9$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-1$, while in the second equation it is $-3$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-3}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $3$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-3$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(a - b = -6)\\cdot (-3); -7a - 3b = 9\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3a + 3b &= 18 \\\\\n-7a - 3b &= 9 \\\\\n(-3a - 7a) &= (18 + 9) \\\\\n-10a &= 27\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-3}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508354 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39a6814c-18ed-51c5-ac72-0b9e8d2d7b22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508276} {:answer/id #uuid "b370d6a5-ae0f-513a-be14-2ead2c5dd0ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508338}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508338} :answer-field/id #uuid "15446ed6-06ee-5e8f-b9db-fb23758c2828" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508257} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e3b6170-053d-5e20-bf03-eb7b7f0b9b9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508271} {:answer/id #uuid "34c59b71-7028-5a50-90c2-416e17328ce0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508274} {:answer/id #uuid "898c0b7e-ab07-55a0-9d3e-8d2228d97878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508323} {:answer/id #uuid "8e9898c4-dfc7-5d09-b10e-60992932dae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508325}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508271} :answer-field/id #uuid "5245f9d9-ac94-562c-8092-471960c6d9fc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508292}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d1ff7503-ea2c-53d8-b2dc-feb812e688fc" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{6x - y = 8; -6x + 2y = 6$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $y$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $y$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $-1$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}2}$, then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $-2$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $2$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(6x - y = 8)\\cdot (2); -6x + 2y = 6\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12x - 2y &= 16 \\\\\n-6x + 2y &= 6 \\\\\n(12x - 6x) &= (16 + 6) \\\\\n6x &= 22\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $y$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "225d1f98-8b27-555d-afa6-e6d941ada34c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508264} {:answer/id #uuid "dc1678d3-65a7-531d-aee9-ccee73215a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508356} {:answer/id #uuid "dfcb8d2b-1f63-5290-bbaf-e02572a87ce1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508357} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a4499a-ae96-5717-b6b6-6daef56eb4cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508366}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508264} :answer-field/id #uuid "07170df4-3002-5d99-8a83-98dd811ef120" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21b689ce-4bcb-548c-8656-608257bc0e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508262} {:answer/id #uuid "57d446a3-0af8-50b0-b18a-e196585ca47d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508299}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508262} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e9670cb-e167-5a08-925c-656947a40567" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e241fcce-6c28-5eb1-91b2-aee856170291" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$\\{10a + b = -1; 9a + 5b = -5$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $1$, while in the second equation it is $5$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-5}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $-5$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $5$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(10a + b = -1)\\cdot (-5); 9a + 5b = -5\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-50a - 5b &= 5 \\\\\n9a + 5b &= -5 \\\\\n(-50a + 9a) &= (5 - 5) \\\\\n-41a &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-5}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09e8579d-b157-52e9-b7ed-5985f9e85259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508248} {:answer/id #uuid "134fb8c9-6ede-56c5-bc4e-c5e8ccaabe65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508255} {:answer/id #uuid "d09d4f07-de21-5249-aa7b-ff1686f1e146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508353} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e111be-bf81-5801-bc93-3b2bad662b63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508361}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508248} :answer-field/id #uuid "074e8cbb-4ae9-5dfc-ad31-766133a53fe3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508246} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e0e218a-1bf4-5098-b918-d285259aca08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508324} {:answer/id #uuid "d9f60b70-b8c2-5448-9297-4b52ef616717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508355}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508324} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d1c3c66-66ba-5111-9e0a-80d446b48de7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e58c3e5b-b391-5afd-9ee6-da3df80ea5cd" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$\\{a - 3b = -6; -7a - 6b = 9$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-3$, while in the second equation it is $-6$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-2}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-6$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(a - 3b = -6)\\cdot (-2); -7a - 6b = 9\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2a + 6b &= 12 \\\\\n-7a - 6b &= 9 \\\\\n(-2a - 7a) &= (12 + 9) \\\\\n-9a &= 21\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-2}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2830d30e-f96c-5c09-a79c-8a94e978b292" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508266} {:answer/id #uuid "5518e6b8-b214-5f7b-a5de-7f4b43b00897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508295} {:answer/id #uuid "82fdb308-ba8c-5c51-a928-c4e4aa5c60e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508318} {:answer/id #uuid "a7870df0-e865-550b-8098-64365d920e80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508335}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508335} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cba64b5-9bf1-503e-b1b2-39e507432e1a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508278} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5000535-be94-5ca1-b227-8c4b08b24908" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508344} {:answer/id #uuid "fa2063e0-c497-5fb3-8b39-0ed66ba354d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508374}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508374} :answer-field/id #uuid "4689c9a4-33eb-5422-8dc1-46ed14684c4f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508283}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f40ec0f3-3ce5-52b3-a3e7-9ca324b7f03c" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{5a - 4b = 6; 8a - 12b = -6$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-4$, while in the second equation it is $-12$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-3}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $12$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-12$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(5a - 4b = 6)\\cdot (-3); 8a - 12b = -6\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-15a + 12b &= -18 \\\\\n8a - 12b &= -6 \\\\\n(-15a + 8a) &= (-18 - 6) \\\\\n-7a &= -24\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-3}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "012d1788-aae6-5b3f-9a33-32cfe9441bb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508392} {:answer/id #uuid "82649ab6-63e2-5e38-9a54-9307deefdeb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508581} {:answer/id #uuid "8b82b948-2752-5af9-8b4b-7dbe6940b437" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508598} {:answer/id #uuid "f1e16c77-b35b-5b8b-82d8-51637fcbbe74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508781}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508581} :answer-field/id #uuid "4046a4d7-d1ee-512c-8f22-ac17abe07653" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508831} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58ca67c6-ef0f-5fd0-bbf0-abeced525206" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508521} {:answer/id #uuid "8c9c819a-e67f-55f7-ae5e-0327e8b580c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508602}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508521} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e78a58b-7fed-5d4a-8336-150e88af3ff3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "09338f11-6e50-5f7e-baa9-764c66288045" :question/math-academy-id "q-238044" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+y &=8 \\\\ 8x-7y &=25\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $y$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $y,$ multiply the \n{{field-1}} \nequation by \n{{field-2}}, \nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $1,$ while in the second equation it is $-7.$ \n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $7,$ then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $7,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $-7$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}(\\,-5x+y &=8\\,)\\,\\times (7) \\\\ 8x-7y &=25\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-35x+7y &=56 \\\\ 8x-7y &=25\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-35x+\\cancel{7y} & =56 \\\\ 8x-\\cancel{7y} & =25 \\\\ (-35x+8x) & =(56+25) \\\\ -27x & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*To eliminate $y,$ multiply the $\\text{first}$ equation by $7,$ and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508932 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "184b7ab4-4868-5106-9bdf-4e1438c33364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508425} {:answer/id #uuid "4662f5b1-a02f-591b-952a-acc6e7eaed94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508495} {:answer/id #uuid "62b5b5df-e1f1-5779-aade-7a55fb1642e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508539} {:answer/id #uuid "bffa8226-fe91-5e80-8884-d0fbe91ee966" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508683}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508539} :answer-field/id #uuid "22d35b8c-5919-5861-973d-60696f665ffd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a15f6018-6390-5ae8-8699-d85026a934d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508631} {:answer/id #uuid "aea80158-002e-503d-aa81-d682984720c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508653}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508631} :answer-field/id #uuid "6752cba9-1654-5c73-9d09-080f3eb8532e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5ba7c176-1d51-52ad-ad1b-a588df23024a" :question/math-academy-id "q-238051" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3p+2q &=11 \\\\ p+q &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $q$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $q,$ multiply the \n{{field-1}} \nequation by \n{{field-2}}, \nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $q$ in the first equation is $2,$ while in the second equation it is $1.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-2,$ then the coefficient of $q$ will turn into $-2,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $2$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3p+2q &=11 \\\\ (\\,p+q &=4\\,)\\,\\times (-2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3p+2q &=11 \\\\ -2p-2q &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $q$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}3p+\\cancel{2q} & =11 \\\\ -2p-\\cancel{2q} & =-8 \\\\ (3p-2p) & =(11-8) \\\\ p & =3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*To eliminate $q,$ multiply the $\\text{second}$ equation by $-2,$ and add the equations*."}] :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192656 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192587 :question/id #uuid "f20f46d9-b799-57a2-90bc-12e6593e8655" :question/math-academy-id "e-13999" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y &=8 \\\\ x-2y &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $2,$ while in the second equation it is $1.$\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-2,$ then the $x$-coefficient will become $-2,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $2$ in the first equation.\n![](images/a7/a7e5f9f09d67dd14a4797e5675585973e3aafeb1ee96e9021d245f49ce9c1c7e.svg)\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{2x}+3y & =8 \\\\ \\cancel{-2x}+4y & =6 \\\\ (3y+4y) & =(8+6) \\\\ 7y & =14 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = 2.$ However, we still need to find $x.$ To do this, we substitute $y = 2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}x-2y & =-3 \\\\ x-2(2) & =-3 \\\\ x-4 & =-3 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=1, \\,y=2,$ which can be expressed as $(1,2).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dbf4e1a-2c87-562d-8c4d-41fd32e79b86" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509123 :question-generator/id #uuid "a2ef49f5-dfc4-5fb1-b890-7cb7bc96039a" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186192656.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9dc4fdb-fc7f-57b9-bbcb-171440bb6b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191189} {:answer/id #uuid "7891246f-146f-5da4-be15-343b7425f61f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508564} {:answer/id #uuid "8468d23b-6f42-50bf-9e79-d910d35e0ee2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508587} {:answer/id #uuid "ac47150e-5e39-5c69-9314-ddb4609e8210" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508651} {:answer/id #uuid "f55c1c33-5ff5-5f10-90f5-08f56a27906c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508791}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186191189} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d02a81e-fa71-57d8-a298-b58e206ffcea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4c0138a9-c275-57a0-80c9-430f32b2f421" :question/math-academy-id "q-18787" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y &=0 \\\\ 2x-3y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $x.$*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $x$-coefficient in the first equation is $4,$ while in the second equation it is $2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-2,$ then the $x$-coefficient will become $-4,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y &=0 \\\\ (\\,2x-3y &=2\\,)\\,\\times (-2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y &=0 \\\\ -4x+6y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{4x}-5y & =0 \\\\ -\\cancel{4x}+6y & =-4 \\\\ (-5y+6y) & =(0-4) \\\\ y & =-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y=-4.$ However, we still need to find $x.$ To do this, we substitute $y=-4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}4x-5y & =0 \\\\ 4x-5(-4) & =0 \\\\ 4x+20 & =0 \\\\ 4x & =-20 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-5,\\,y=-4,$ which can be expressed as $(-5,-4).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193236 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "1baa2398-4954-5c79-9541-1319e47e02cd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191226} {:answer-field/id #uuid "652cda5c-8a31-5ce3-bccf-786c2da038cc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191227}] :question/id #uuid "96c8f94a-3d88-537c-8d5d-fa47a28c510f" :question/math-academy-id "q-208816" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n${4x + 3y = 5; - x + 7y =-9$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}} $$,\n{{field-2}}\n$)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dddb3dd-6633-5329-a169-4b39e35735ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508628}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508628} :answer-field/id #uuid "2696769d-e344-58f2-b122-e8524fb62262" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5032cf38-f7e1-5f19-b56e-8d84bbbcec8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508509}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508509} :answer-field/id #uuid "2adc4195-f1d2-500e-8a09-82e4a8b25e53" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4775db8b-54b5-507a-83b4-6fee15253323" :question/math-academy-id "q-238082" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+13y &=21 \\\\ 2x+6y &=12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y)$ to this system is $($\n{{field-1}}$\\,,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the  first  equation is $6,$ while in the second equation it is $2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-3,$ then the $x$-coefficient will become $-6,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $6$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+13y &=21 \\\\ (\\,2x+6y &=12\\,)\\,\\times (-3)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+13y &=21 \\\\ -6x-18y &=-36\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{6x}+13y & =21 \\\\ -\\cancel{6x}-18y & =-36 \\\\ (13y-18y) & =(21-36) \\\\ -5y & =-15 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y=3.$ However, we still need to find $x.$ To do this, we substitute $y=3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+13y & =21 \\\\ 6x+13(3) & =21 \\\\ 6x+39 & =21 \\\\ 6x & =-18 \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-3,\\,y=3,$ which can be expressed as $(-3,3).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509050 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5ee4058-4cb0-5815-af4f-31cb5f7f4b9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509104}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509104} :answer-field/id #uuid "491f86ca-62f3-5ea9-8428-178689de26c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509073} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "accbd167-8445-5f77-b722-a480de8d9a7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509102}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509102} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0ddcf7e-8326-53ea-93be-7d843009b320" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509096}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "02c41293-f116-502f-be60-22954dd650e1" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{-8x + 5y = 1; -2x - 7y = 25$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $-8$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-4$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-8$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-8x + 5y = 1; (-2x - 7y = 25) \\cdot (-4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 5y &= 1 \\\\\n8x + 28y &= -100 \\\\\n(5y + 28y) &= (1 - 100) \\\\\n33y &= -99 \\\\\ny &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = -3$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = -3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - 7y &= 25 \\\\\n-2x - 7(-3) &= 25 \\\\\n-2x + 21 &= 25 \\\\\n-2x &= 4 \\\\\nx &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-2, \\,y=-3$, which can be expressed as $(-2,-3)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509058 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72fa66fd-476b-567c-997f-57d2e464fff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{737}{36}, - \\frac{79}{18})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509085} {:answer/id #uuid "738e474f-8d81-5bf6-bc84-52f4e7d52157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(17, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509086} {:answer/id #uuid "bd5dcb71-ce6e-543f-8d84-cd26efc72f79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{113}{9}, - \\frac{11}{9})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509105} {:answer/id #uuid "c9adc298-4dc0-5aaf-b90e-98f63bda9ce1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(77, -27)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509110} {:answer/id #uuid "cd44a84c-9d0c-5c1f-a7ba-d0979b60fd66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509112}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509112} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b8157cd-7759-5311-a70d-1e44f2700470" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "258cf739-9da3-523a-9e45-9eb6c6ac19c9" :question/problem "Find the solution $(a, b)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$\\{2a + 5b = 19; 14a - b = 25$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $a$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $a$ in the first equation is $2$, while in the second equation it is $14$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $-7$, then the $a$-coefficient will become $-14$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $14$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(2a + 5b = 19) \\cdot (-7); 14a - b = 25\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $a$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-14a - 35b &= -133 \\\\\n14a - b &= 25 \\\\\n(-35b - b) &= (-133 + 25) \\\\\n-36b &= -108 \\\\\nb &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $b = 3$. However, we still need to find $a$. To do this, we substitute $b = 3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a + 5b &= 19 \\\\\n2a + 5(3) &= 19 \\\\\n2a + 15 &= 19 \\\\\n2a &= 4 \\\\\na &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=2, \\,b=3$, which can be expressed as $(2,3)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "079d8e57-e723-5341-8dde-001d8b14de99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509052}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509052} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa48b9e4-f99c-585d-9f9c-fcfbc501054e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509101} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "338fa4ef-f1d5-5f60-94f0-02b5a1eb96c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509064}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509064} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc5d5aa6-a936-5fba-8da0-69bd505be987" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3584fccc-ff52-560b-affb-117ca9035e1b" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{12s - t = -10; 2s - 5t = 8$\n\nFind the solution $(s, t)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $s$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $12$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-6$, then the $s$-coefficient will become $-12$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $12$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{12s - t = -10; (2s - 5t = 8) \\cdot (-6)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12s - t &= -10 \\\\\n-12s + 30t &= -48 \\\\\n(-t + 30t) &= (-10 - 48) \\\\\n29t &= -58 \\\\\nt &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $t = -2$. However, we still need to find $s$. To do this, we substitute $t = -2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2s - 5t &= 8 \\\\\n2s - 5(-2) &= 8 \\\\\n2s + 10 &= 8 \\\\\n2s &= -2 \\\\\ns &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $s=-1, \\,t=-2$, which can be expressed as $(-1,-2)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509068 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1f2ef5d-7d4c-5874-a963-39537f63090c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509097}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509097} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ad33376-4060-5d96-9e58-c7394afcbf4f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509075} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7d55bbb-17db-553d-bf14-bb89392e7ac8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509120}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509120} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4fe934f-8389-5fa9-ac8c-55f6141852fe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3848697a-49af-57cf-80a1-3aeaa90cbfd0" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{2x + 3y = 1; 14x - 3y = -17$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $2$, while in the second equation it is $14$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $-7$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $-14$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $14$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(2x + 3y = 1) \\cdot (-7); 14x - 3y = -17\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-14x - 21y &= -7 \\\\\n14x - 3y &= -17 \\\\\n(-21y - 3y) &= (-7 - 17) \\\\\n-24y &= -24 \\\\\ny &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = 1$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = 1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + 3y &= 1 \\\\\n2x + 3(1) &= 1 \\\\\n2x + 3 &= 1 \\\\\n2x &= -2 \\\\\nx &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-1, \\,y=1$, which can be expressed as $(-1,1)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "364f9c8a-cb70-5cde-84ad-03c48868d69b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509067}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509067} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ae32b84-e095-5a2f-9172-81edb43c515f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509094} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30017ff9-b626-5f0f-96bf-3f60d887385e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509061}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509061} :answer-field/id #uuid "c437e509-1b3a-5a4b-872f-05ce93198e77" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509107}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "66c662cf-af7a-5ce7-907d-2fc15145c8ec" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{9a + 4b = 16; -3a - 4b = 8$\n\nFind the solution $(a, b)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $a$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $a$ in the first equation is $9$, while in the second equation it is $-3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $3$, then the $a$-coefficient will become $-9$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $9$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{9a + 4b = 16; (-3a - 4b = 8) \\cdot (3)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $a$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9a + 4b &= 16 \\\\\n-9a - 12b &= 24 \\\\\n(4b - 12b) &= (16 + 24) \\\\\n-8b &= 40 \\\\\nb &= -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $b = -5$. However, we still need to find $a$. To do this, we substitute $b = -5$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3a - 4b &= 8 \\\\\n-3a - 4(-5) &= 8 \\\\\n-3a + 20 &= 8 \\\\\n-3a &= -12 \\\\\na &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=4, \\,b=-5$, which can be expressed as $(4,-5)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509087 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f96d8b6a-e305-583b-9f12-0bde0306eb41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509121}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509121} :answer-field/id #uuid "4abb445a-53b1-5dac-8db1-19d2b720a47b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509074} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6af2d8cd-fb27-51d6-805e-b4b55efe8db1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509082}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509082} :answer-field/id #uuid "d13464d6-06b5-572e-a588-9d420ee2218d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7b0730ae-94df-51c2-9122-80a657d5c130" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{6s + 7t = -17; -s + 5t = 9$\n\nFind the solution $(s, t)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $s$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $6$, while in the second equation it is $-1$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $6$, then the $s$-coefficient will become $-6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $6$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{6s + 7t = -17; (-s + 5t = 9) \\cdot (6)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6s + 7t &= -17 \\\\\n-6s + 30t &= 54 \\\\\n(7t + 30t) &= (-17 + 54) \\\\\n37t &= 37 \\\\\nt &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $t = 1$. However, we still need to find $s$. To do this, we substitute $t = 1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-s + 5t &= 9 \\\\\n-s + 5(1) &= 9 \\\\\n-s + 5 &= 9 \\\\\ns &= -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $s=-4, \\,t=1$, which can be expressed as $(-4,1)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509093 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64612dae-60be-5da8-a58f-b92a90c02672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509080}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509080} :answer-field/id #uuid "25eacce8-21cd-5065-b87b-8364d07c64a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509059} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e23b228-36a0-5619-a7b7-a3921c993c40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509053}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509053} :answer-field/id #uuid "82814543-c725-5b0a-b1ee-c015e7918acc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9719f6ce-a725-5fda-8dba-4e72f19011f6" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{8x + y = -12; 2x - 7y = -32$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $8$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-4$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $-8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $8$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{8x + y = -12; (2x - 7y = -32) \\cdot (-4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8x + y &= -12 \\\\\n-8x + 28y &= 128 \\\\\n(y + 28y) &= (-12 + 128) \\\\\n29y &= 116 \\\\\ny &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = 4$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = 4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x - 7y &= -32 \\\\\n2x - 7(4) &= -32 \\\\\n2x - 28 &= -32 \\\\\n2x &= -4 \\\\\nx &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-2, \\,y=4$, which can be expressed as $(-2,4)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509100 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22b8f003-4864-5c70-95fe-d2b3563f85ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7, -2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509056} {:answer/id #uuid "329f0e6d-30d3-5076-b0f7-a3bfcc97b663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{4}, - \\frac{3}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509063} {:answer/id #uuid "3d9aae26-9eaa-543f-ad73-d4b0cc4ce5d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{29}{5}, \\frac{8}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509069} {:answer/id #uuid "52ca360c-fb47-5f69-899f-de261ec2a7c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{11}{4}, - \\frac{5}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509077} {:answer/id #uuid "f52d4e69-0b6e-526b-ab03-608e96f2bffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5, -2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509118}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509118} :answer-field/id #uuid "4740f935-4cde-5928-81e3-2873eb56ade9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a75817b8-4e26-5edd-a706-c4d036e41293" :question/problem "Find the solution $(a, b)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$\\{-5a - 7b = -11; -a - 3b = 1$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $a$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $a$ in the first equation is $-5$, while in the second equation it is $-1$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-5$, then the $a$-coefficient will become $5$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-5$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-5a - 7b = -11; (-a - 3b = 1) \\cdot (-5)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $a$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5a - 7b &= -11 \\\\\n5a + 15b &= -5 \\\\\n(-7b + 15b) &= (-11 - 5) \\\\\n8b &= -16 \\\\\nb &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $b = -2$. However, we still need to find $a$. To do this, we substitute $b = -2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-a - 3b &= 1 \\\\\n-a - 3(-2) &= 1 \\\\\n-a + 6 &= 1 \\\\\na &= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=5, \\,b=-2$, which can be expressed as $(5,-2)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509103 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04912936-0284-538a-a031-970ac8ce1261" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1077}{16}, \\frac{123}{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509051} {:answer/id #uuid "305a3950-6485-5d6d-9a0b-5b40b1148ce8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1257}{41}, \\frac{201}{41})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509062} {:answer/id #uuid "4372d300-0380-515a-a5b7-c7ff3a05051f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-24, -3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509071} {:answer/id #uuid "86db7400-28e3-565a-b953-d96d40f7af0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3, -3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509090} {:answer/id #uuid "fc181fc8-9703-58c0-a004-a3247d964adb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1569}{82}, \\frac{66}{41})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509122}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509090} :answer-field/id #uuid "891fd9c0-9987-5b47-b883-682276b9d5c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b3065a5a-e33d-5a8d-955c-b55d1f00fd62" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$\\{-12x - y = 39; -2x - 7y = 27$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $x$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $-12$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-6$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $12$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-12$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-12x - y = 39; (-2x - 7y = 27) \\cdot (-6)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x - y &= 39 \\\\\n12x + 42y &= -162 \\\\\n(-y + 42y) &= (39 - 162) \\\\\n41y &= -123 \\\\\ny &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = -3$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = -3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - 7y &= 27 \\\\\n-2x - 7(-3) &= 27 \\\\\n-2x + 21 &= 27 \\\\\n-2x &= 6 \\\\\nx &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-3, \\,y=-3$, which can be expressed as $(-3,-3)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509106 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c67e1be-bd46-5ffa-8808-2973f101d188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509079}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509079} :answer-field/id #uuid "83a992ad-facb-5e3e-9fe4-d815a0ee6bea" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509089} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a45d5d1a-0ddd-57b6-94a4-fadb72cadada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509098}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509098} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9a7d8bf-c851-5b7c-950c-16ced188e9d5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c26af310-f3be-5785-a8b6-74feb81edc70" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{21u - 4v = -25; 3u + v = -2$\n\nFind the solution $(u, v)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $u$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $u$ in the first equation is $21$, while in the second equation it is $3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-7$, then the $u$-coefficient will become $-21$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $21$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{21u - 4v = -25; (3u + v = -2) \\cdot (-7)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $u$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n21u - 4v &= -25 \\\\\n-21u - 7v &= 14 \\\\\n(-4v - 7v) &= (-25 + 14) \\\\\n-11v &= -11 \\\\\nv &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $v = 1$. However, we still need to find $u$. To do this, we substitute $v = 1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3u + v &= -2 \\\\\n3u + (1) &= -2 \\\\\n3u + 1 &= -2 \\\\\n3u &= -3 \\\\\nu &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=-1, \\,v=1$, which can be expressed as $(-1,1)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7242848c-3d45-59cd-b531-0ff9de9e07b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509084}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509084} :answer-field/id #uuid "580f77f4-bb2d-5fe9-8c7a-de148eb78cf9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e215f69-7281-5f0a-b1ad-ca14eb46e414" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509070}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509070} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f423d74-9353-5d5c-8788-04c8f0bcc44d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509095}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cd3b4b3f-b020-5169-9586-17768134232d" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{-4x + 5y = 10; x + 6y = -17$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $-4$, while in the second equation it is $1$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $4$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $4$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-4$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-4x + 5y = 10; (x + 6y = -17) \\cdot (4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x + 5y &= 10 \\\\\n4x + 24y &= -68 \\\\\n(5y + 24y) &= (10 - 68) \\\\\n29y &= -58 \\\\\ny &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = -2$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = -2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx + 6y &= -17 \\\\\nx + 6(-2) &= -17 \\\\\nx - 12 &= -17 \\\\\nx &= -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-5, \\,y=-2$, which can be expressed as $(-5,-2)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509114 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12813af6-c484-54ac-9bee-0b9a07a1472c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509055}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509055} :answer-field/id #uuid "23b567cb-7d1b-5181-9ccc-bcb98c7d98fc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509057} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e284178-f4bc-505f-90f2-2ff6238fd5eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509054}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509054} :answer-field/id #uuid "f538230e-e945-5377-a73a-dcace5a3652d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d400f619-bf7d-5b12-8de8-ccc69c639d78" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{s + 3t = -14; 3s - t = -2$\n\nFind the solution $(s, t)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $s$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $1$, while in the second equation it is $3$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $-3$, then the $s$-coefficient will become $-3$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $3$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(s + 3t = -14) \\cdot (-3); 3s - t = -2\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3s - 9t &= 42 \\\\\n3s - t &= -2 \\\\\n(-9t - t) &= (42 - 2) \\\\\n-10t &= 40 \\\\\nt &= -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $t = -4$. However, we still need to find $s$. To do this, we substitute $t = -4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ns + 3t &= -14 \\\\\ns + 3(-4) &= -14 \\\\\ns - 12 &= -14 \\\\\ns &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $s=-2, \\,t=-4$, which can be expressed as $(-2,-4)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509115 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2faf14ba-bba7-51c7-9edf-cecfc41c14b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7, 17)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509060} {:answer/id #uuid "341043a8-156f-5366-9a35-b7d38e44dfa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{11}{14}, \\frac{10}{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509065} {:answer/id #uuid "4aedf174-56a2-5192-a1db-d3ba0e5fc303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1, 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509076} {:answer/id #uuid "9632d4fa-7a1a-5278-a13a-d1e219be729e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{19}{4}, \\frac{25}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509092} {:answer/id #uuid "d97fab02-f410-5d26-9830-684eabd5761d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4, 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509116}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509076} :answer-field/id #uuid "c554ee94-9b1e-56b7-bcce-cdb86ae35436" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d579d3ab-2a4e-5b62-a685-7b2b44091ebf" :question/problem "Find the solution $(s, t)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$\\{8s + 6t = 22; 2s + t = 3$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $s$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $8$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-4$, then the $s$-coefficient will become $-8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $8$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{8s + 6t = 22; (2s + t = 3) \\cdot (-4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8s + 6t &= 22 \\\\\n-8s - 4t &= -12 \\\\\n(6t - 4t) &= (22 - 12) \\\\\n2t &= 10 \\\\\nt &= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $t = 5$. However, we still need to find $s$. To do this, we substitute $t = 5$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2s + t &= 3 \\\\\n2s + (5) &= 3 \\\\\n2s + 5 &= 3 \\\\\n2s &= -2 \\\\\ns &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $s=-1, \\,t=5$, which can be expressed as $(-1,5)$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations by Eliminating the First Variable"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192657 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192588 :question/id #uuid "990e3660-dfd7-50fa-b60b-0478ff02a073" :question/math-academy-id "e-14002" :question/problem "Find the solution $(u,v)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5u-6v &=3 \\\\ -3u+2v &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $v$-coefficient in the first equation is $-6,$ while in the second equation it is $2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $3,$ then the $v$-coefficient will become $6,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $-6$ in the first equation.\n![](images/e7/e701d299976539abdbbe6e9c311c2db14c23cca6817c5a3de5b5c05a95760d99.svg)\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $v$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}5u-\\cancel{6v} & =3 \\\\ -9u+\\cancel{6v} & =-15 \\\\ (5u-9u) & =(3-15) \\\\ -4u & =-12 \\\\ u & =3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $u = 3.$ However, we still need to find $v.$ To do this, we substitute $u = 3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3u+2v & =-5 \\\\ -3(3)+2v & =-5 \\\\ -9+2v & =-5 \\\\ 2v & =4 \\\\ v & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u = 3, \\,v = 2,$ which can be expressed as $(3,2).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "238f847f-5009-5183-b9bd-b8e136f0ba4d" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509345 :question-generator/id #uuid "24c9299c-e1f2-5131-9fa7-77c01dfe4bb1" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186192657.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193212 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d19e5318-830b-5397-b5d5-db4b2ea4edd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191159} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d7c2ec-2218-5685-bd6d-a27b265e6cce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191160} {:answer/id #uuid "41d06511-304d-52ec-8660-cebfa1226e4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3, 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191161} {:answer/id #uuid "68ebd117-4cb9-5c3f-911c-a45f8215fa93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191162} {:answer/id #uuid "73de3fc5-e6cf-5c66-bccb-fd58d2b8db1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191163}] :answer-field/id #uuid "84dcebbe-0ca8-598a-800e-4c91899feb7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191158}] :question/id #uuid "ac5edd25-6b22-5574-95a5-6e2d817dd860" :question/math-academy-id "q-170145" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n${3x - 2y =-1; 4x + y =-5$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $y$.*"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5deaa590-2cc0-5e91-b357-5a9ea981fe20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508529}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508529} :answer-field/id #uuid "24fdb15c-a8b3-5277-abc3-5f3c2cfa726d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191552} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6e8f613-08b6-5743-b480-77cc2a7e2ff1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508699}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508699} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a2a4186-c9b8-58ca-9163-304a07832933" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "659bfd82-a0b2-5112-81eb-2185b857af31" :question/math-academy-id "q-238087" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+2y &=11 \\\\ 7x+4y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x,y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $y.$\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}$\\,,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $2,$ while in the second equation it is $4.$ \n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $-2,$ then the $y$-coefficient will become $-4,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}(\\,-5x+2y &=11\\,)\\,\\times (-2) \\\\ 7x+4y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}10x-4y &=-22 \\\\ 7x+4y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10x-\\cancel{4y} & =-22 \\\\ 7x+\\cancel{4y} & =5 \\\\ (10x+7x) & =(-22+5) \\\\ 17x & =-17 \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x=-1.$ However, we still need to find $y.$ To do this, we substitute $x=-1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+4y & =5 \\\\ 7(-1)+4y & =5 \\\\ -7+4y & =5 \\\\ 4y & =12 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-1,\\,y=3,$ which can be expressed as $(-1,3).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508927 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60ff1fa4-ffc7-5336-b3af-c476f0ceefb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508536} {:answer/id #uuid "6d3b6243-75d7-5af0-9491-17de5aeb8a29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508553} {:answer/id #uuid "7e050490-5650-55a2-bbaf-c33b2adf2dd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508573} {:answer/id #uuid "c386a187-6f74-5af7-a28a-842f181e5f36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508690} {:answer/id #uuid "f8157de3-2831-5e1e-a4bb-0158173f239a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508798}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508536} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1429b72-180d-5d2a-ae39-57cc2cf7b25c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4c472f9d-cfda-5414-a840-ee6d18544bcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-170159" :question/problem "Find the solution $(p,q)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3p+2q &=11 \\\\ 5p+4q &=19\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $q.$*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $q$-coefficient in the first equation is $2,$ while in the second equation it is $4.$ \n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $-2,$ then the $q$-coefficient will become $-4,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}(\\,3p+2q &=11\\,)\\,\\times (-2) \\\\ 5p+4q &=19\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6p-4q &=-22 \\\\ 5p+4q &=19\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $q$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-6p-\\cancel{4q} & =-22 \\\\ 5p+\\cancel{4q} & =19 \\\\ (-6p+5p) & =(-22+19) \\\\ -p & =-3 \\\\ p & =3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $p=3.$ However, we still need to find $q.$ To do this, we substitute $p=3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p+2q & =11 \\\\ 3(3)+2q & =11 \\\\ 9+2q & =11 \\\\ 2q & =2 \\\\ q & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=3,\\,q=1,$ which can be expressed as $(3,1).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509267 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91e9c308-67f3-5e17-a945-9f7ca8b964e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509311}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509311} :answer-field/id #uuid "147b96a0-420d-536f-930a-bf1ab6057f76" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509266} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fee1e55-5f1d-5256-8a99-8662fe215f83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509268}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509268} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7e7709b-4144-5bdd-89e3-266ed5cdd337" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "15551398-1d65-5cfc-9388-3441da458ef3" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+y&=16\\\\-7x-6y&=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $y$.\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $,$ {{field-2}} $)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $1$, while in the second equation it is $-6$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $6$, then the $y$-coefficient will become $6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-6$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{ \\left(5x+y=16\\right)\\cdot (6); -7x-6y=-4\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n30x+6y&=96 \\\\\n-7x-6y&=-4 \\\\\n(30x-7x)&=(96-4) \\\\\n23x&=92 \\\\\nx&=4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x = 4$. However, we still need to find $y$. To do this, we substitute $x = 4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x+y&=16 \\\\\n5(4)+y&=16 \\\\\n20+y&=16 \\\\\ny&=-4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is\n\n$$\nx = 4, \\,y = -4\n$$\n\nwhich can be expressed as $(4,-4)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509270 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "200edcc6-55df-50a4-aa4a-486132c110af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{28}{11},- \\frac{339}{22})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509269} {:answer/id #uuid "59eca543-875a-5f9c-906c-2227556ef87f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509292} {:answer/id #uuid "9bae6aad-69de-515b-ae98-f68c8a8cd5c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{15}{11},- \\frac{124}{11})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509315} {:answer/id #uuid "c8204af7-b37e-5cf3-8cb6-a7dd64791ca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509329} {:answer/id #uuid "fb2229f3-7217-5ef8-ada8-8b297feb7340" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509343}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509329} :answer-field/id #uuid "f87fcfbe-ec51-5267-986b-e924e05d49d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "21904fad-7e59-5888-9a6b-ef099e3648bc" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+6y&=-17\\\\-7x+2y&=-13\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $y$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $6$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-3$, then the $y$-coefficient will become $-6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $6$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{ x+6y=-17; \\left(-7x+2y=-13\\right)\\cdot (-3)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx+6y&=-17 \\\\\n21x-6y&=39 \\\\\n(x+21x)&=(-17+39) \\\\\n22x&=22 \\\\\nx&=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x = 1$. However, we still need to find $y$. To do this, we substitute $x = 1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-7x+2y&=-13 \\\\\n-7(1)+2y&=-13 \\\\\n-7+2y&=-13 \\\\\n2y&=-6 \\\\\ny&=-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is\n\n$$\nx = 1, \\,y = -3\n$$\n\nwhich can be expressed as $(1,-3)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509271 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f908001-8c0e-5ad5-bf2c-a4aae8e1a691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509264}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509264} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc24fa13-ffeb-5ff7-9dbb-b1d479e2964b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509330} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e86f70f-2c51-5c48-9d22-0d5dc6889c88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509263}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509263} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5fd3803-15e2-50c5-94bb-4bdef29b8a99" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "23b70eba-8c0c-5171-b139-0ac2370d20a6" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+14y&=-36\\\\-7x-2y&=-20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $y$.\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $,$ {{field-2}} $)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $14$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $7$, then the $y$-coefficient will become $-14$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $14$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{ 5x+14y=-36; \\left(-7x-2y=-20\\right)\\cdot (7)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x+14y&=-36 \\\\\n-49x-14y&=-140 \\\\\n(5x-49x)&=(-36-140) \\\\\n-44x&=-176 \\\\\nx&=4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x = 4$. However, we still need to find $y$. To do this, we substitute $x = 4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-7x-2y&=-20 \\\\\n-7(4)-2y&=-20 \\\\\n-28-2y&=-20 \\\\\n-2y&=8 \\\\\ny&=-4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is\n\n$$\nx = 4, \\,y = -4\n$$\n\nwhich can be expressed as $(4,-4)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509278 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b382fd6-c1bc-58a5-ab3b-203bfcd1d3f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509275} {:answer/id #uuid "35155a6e-f543-56cc-895d-88462084d35c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509277} {:answer/id #uuid "8ee68739-5943-5dba-a7b3-6a408d7f228a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509309} {:answer/id #uuid "bf7dc056-edde-5f96-a671-5ccf85ff5755" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{64}{5},- \\frac{99}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509324} {:answer/id #uuid "f8dcd307-0ccd-537f-902c-16a48c2e11dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509342}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509277} :answer-field/id #uuid "76d0f030-a9e9-5940-9a6d-793769aabcc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3775b5ec-0d42-5ee6-ba36-8700f462d97a" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+y&=-7\\\\x-6y&=22\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $y$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $1$, while in the second equation it is $-6$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $6$, then the $y$-coefficient will become $6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-6$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{ \\left(-x+y=-7\\right)\\cdot (6); x-6y=22\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-6x+6y&=-42 \\\\\nx-6y&=22 \\\\\n(-6x+x)&=(-42+22) \\\\\n-5x&=-20 \\\\\nx&=4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x = 4$. However, we still need to find $y$. To do this, we substitute $x = 4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x+y&=-7 \\\\\n-1(4)+y&=-7 \\\\\n-4+y&=-7 \\\\\ny&=-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is\n\n$$\nx = 4, \\,y = -3\n$$\n\nwhich can be expressed as $(4,-3)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509288 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26cfe277-3842-5747-9ee0-6c4247fead55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509273} {:answer/id #uuid "450b54a2-ea5c-555a-b4d6-fe9b7a919372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,27)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509283} {:answer/id #uuid "97dffbe1-1bb5-5124-8577-4fb6de014f06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{23}{13},\\frac{264}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509313} {:answer/id #uuid "a2934f92-f656-5bd6-8747-1b6db11bc275" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509316} {:answer/id #uuid "f434a981-e2a2-536d-8559-c0efa231bcb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{68}{13},\\frac{399}{13})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509340}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509273} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b38b033-45ad-5b3e-b165-1a07d9c9cdc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "575d3d25-ee48-560a-beb0-60eb637f5795" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+4y&=8\\\\3x+y&=15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $y$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $4$, while in the second equation it is $1$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-4$, then the $y$-coefficient will become $-4$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{ -x+4y=8; \\left(3x+y=15\\right)\\cdot (-4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x+4y&=8 \\\\\n-12x-4y&=-60 \\\\\n(-x-12x)&=(8-60) \\\\\n-13x&=-52 \\\\\nx&=4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x = 4$. However, we still need to find $y$. To do this, we substitute $x = 4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x+y&=15 \\\\\n3(4)+y&=15 \\\\\n12+y&=15 \\\\\ny&=3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is\n\n$$\nx = 4, \\,y = 3\n$$\n\nwhich can be expressed as $(4,3)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13e27713-0c32-5160-bf48-8794b4ef56ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509265} {:answer/id #uuid "37d9b91c-a905-57ce-81a0-85f4eccb157f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1}{2},- \\frac{11}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509279} {:answer/id #uuid "82de173e-ffef-54ef-bc13-55db11bad3d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,- \\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509306} {:answer/id #uuid "c1fbed6e-fb34-5ad3-8ef9-483b59c4fa39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509325} {:answer/id #uuid "e6a705a0-e0c3-5f06-aaae-681a63958822" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509337}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509325} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7e82569-1864-5896-a52b-68af45977480" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "78207f23-12ee-53c5-9f78-9395f0921474" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y&=5\\\\7x-6y&=11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $y$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $-2$, while in the second equation it is $-6$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $-3$, then the $y$-coefficient will become $6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-6$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{ \\left(x-2y=5\\right)\\cdot (-3); 7x-6y=11\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x+6y&=-15 \\\\\n7x-6y&=11 \\\\\n(-3x+7x)&=(-15+11) \\\\\n4x&=-4 \\\\\nx&=-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x = -1$. However, we still need to find $y$. To do this, we substitute $x = -1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx-2y&=5 \\\\\n1(-1)-2y&=5 \\\\\n-1-2y&=5 \\\\\n-2y&=6 \\\\\ny&=-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is\n\n$$\nx = -1, \\,y = -3\n$$\n\nwhich can be expressed as $(-1,-3)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30dff6f0-44a2-569f-9cf5-16833973d9d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{48}{43},- \\frac{895}{86})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509276} {:answer/id #uuid "5445dbb7-2643-5c0f-a09e-cd8ccf6fd047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509286} {:answer/id #uuid "6ba4ae51-6c73-5240-afd2-12a95ee94548" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509297} {:answer/id #uuid "77ffeb13-0d3e-595c-929a-d62967cf28a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509301} {:answer/id #uuid "cd313717-399a-59fe-9882-55714ce7fdb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{113}{43},- \\frac{675}{43})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509331}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509301} :answer-field/id #uuid "b210daf5-f7c9-544f-a57c-87c7b7a3a074" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509320}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "888444ab-20f1-5ac7-85e7-9089399fd1bb" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+12y&=-35\\\\-7x+2y&=-13\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $y$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $12$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-6$, then the $y$-coefficient will become $-12$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $12$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{ x+12y=-35; \\left(-7x+2y=-13\\right)\\cdot (-6)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx+12y&=-35 \\\\\n42x-12y&=78 \\\\\n(x+42x)&=(-35+78) \\\\\n43x&=43 \\\\\nx&=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x = 1$. However, we still need to find $y$. To do this, we substitute $x = 1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-7x+2y&=-13 \\\\\n-7(1)+2y&=-13 \\\\\n-7+2y&=-13 \\\\\n2y&=-6 \\\\\ny&=-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is\n\n$$\nx = 1, \\,y = -3\n$$\n\nwhich can be expressed as $(1,-3)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509310 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c580255-e760-5f33-8c6a-2550a573a799" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-22,52)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509262} {:answer/id #uuid "57ef6484-bebb-5270-9134-2a94851e1343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509289} {:answer/id #uuid "65e68218-6593-5454-a9fc-d17eedb52630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{10}{11},- \\frac{8}{11})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509295} {:answer/id #uuid "d7b0f169-c30c-552b-b0d7-efdfc48e9c64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509335} {:answer/id #uuid "eadf7382-2d55-5dc8-a450-064d2a4cf6fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509338}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509289} :answer-field/id #uuid "2658620e-2fcd-55d0-9ddc-b610c83e058d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "90d0118c-789c-54fc-9fd4-a48e58b92b30" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x-2y&=6\\\\3x+10y&=14\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $y$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $-2$, while in the second equation it is $10$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $5$, then the $y$-coefficient will become $-10$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $10$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{ \\left(-5x-2y=6\\right)\\cdot (5); 3x+10y=14\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-25x-10y&=30 \\\\\n3x+10y&=14 \\\\\n(-25x+3x)&=(30+14) \\\\\n-22x&=44 \\\\\nx&=-2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x = -2$. However, we still need to find $y$. To do this, we substitute $x = -2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x-2y&=6 \\\\\n-5(-2)-2y&=6 \\\\\n10-2y&=6 \\\\\n-2y&=-4 \\\\\ny&=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is\n\n$$\nx = -2, \\,y = 2\n$$\n\nwhich can be expressed as $(-2,2)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509318 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d2421c4-3e95-5a88-8c94-267fc39c0f35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509298} {:answer/id #uuid "7135885d-50ad-52a2-b1d8-046d4c8b8464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509299} {:answer/id #uuid "7935b5f6-9317-5d13-a182-f177d4cf51e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,\\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509303} {:answer/id #uuid "7ac1beda-ed4c-5a56-9a2c-7d43cc5905f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509304} {:answer/id #uuid "b920b780-bd99-5c37-9e3d-f93a43c3c601" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509323}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509304} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3a96850-9a06-5e2c-8ce5-899e594c0915" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ad8b1c30-588c-535a-9132-16c79af9dfe2" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+4y&=-1\\\\x+2y&=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $y$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $4$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-2$, then the $y$-coefficient will become $-4$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{ 5x+4y=-1; \\left(x+2y=1\\right)\\cdot (-2)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x+4y&=-1 \\\\\n-2x-4y&=-2 \\\\\n(5x-2x)&=(-1-2) \\\\\n3x&=-3 \\\\\nx&=-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x = -1$. However, we still need to find $y$. To do this, we substitute $x = -1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx+2y&=1 \\\\\n1(-1)+2y&=1 \\\\\n-1+2y&=1 \\\\\n2y&=2 \\\\\ny&=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is\n\n$$\nx = -1, \\,y = 1\n$$\n\nwhich can be expressed as $(-1,1)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66300ce6-b475-5d0f-b089-ac8eec2807a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509296}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509296} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fec54cb-9c85-5252-8582-cea05545c3ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509285} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5709927f-d51f-5749-a92a-072b5998a2f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509287}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509287} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3de5a92-faa1-5773-9a97-9f5b9fa3c657" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c4b00c48-3459-54dd-a97b-4752b54d2e62" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+8y&=-12\\\\-7x-2y&=-20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $y$.\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $,$ {{field-2}} $)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $8$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $4$, then the $y$-coefficient will become $-8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $8$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{ 5x+8y=-12; \\left(-7x-2y=-20\\right)\\cdot (4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x+8y&=-12 \\\\\n-28x-8y&=-80 \\\\\n(5x-28x)&=(-12-80) \\\\\n-23x&=-92 \\\\\nx&=4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x = 4$. However, we still need to find $y$. To do this, we substitute $x = 4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-7x-2y&=-20 \\\\\n-7(4)-2y&=-20 \\\\\n-28-2y&=-20 \\\\\n-2y&=8 \\\\\ny&=-4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is\n\n$$\nx = 4, \\,y = -4\n$$\n\nwhich can be expressed as $(4,-4)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509333 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b4363e1-914f-5143-818c-f9a250cf4675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{9}{19},- \\frac{265}{57})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509280} {:answer/id #uuid "58d587da-c716-5846-9cf4-4ad93c3d7829" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509291} {:answer/id #uuid "93e6532a-ea86-5e9b-b388-cca7bcfcdbde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509312} {:answer/id #uuid "b17056e7-740c-572d-a1a8-6081d649e85d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{95}{3},\\frac{151}{9})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509319} {:answer/id #uuid "d05f6b87-d487-5741-a054-888fc5a7888a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,- \\frac{23}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509332}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509312} :answer-field/id #uuid "07e1e4bf-ace0-570f-9bd6-71262f095a75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509260}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d5c3f388-7843-5364-910c-9e97bb540c6d" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x-3y&=13\\\\5x-21y&=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $y$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $-3$, while in the second equation it is $-21$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $-7$, then the $y$-coefficient will become $21$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-21$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{ \\left(-2x-3y=13\\right)\\cdot (-7); 5x-21y=-4\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n14x+21y&=-91 \\\\\n5x-21y&=-4 \\\\\n(14x+5x)&=(-91-4) \\\\\n19x&=-95 \\\\\nx&=-5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x = -5$. However, we still need to find $y$. To do this, we substitute $x = -5$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x-3y&=13 \\\\\n-2(-5)-3y&=13 \\\\\n10-3y&=13 \\\\\n-3y&=3 \\\\\ny&=-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is\n\n$$\nx = -5, \\,y = -1\n$$\n\nwhich can be expressed as $(-5,-1)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509339 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ecbbb5e-3ed2-528e-830c-64e987e989da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509281} {:answer/id #uuid "42e7ebb4-26b8-5fd9-b9bf-6edb7cf93ed3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509282} {:answer/id #uuid "843072f9-f614-5e55-8bf0-12fd95bdb012" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509307} {:answer/id #uuid "991361f4-364a-57db-97a8-04a5f7037455" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,15)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509314} {:answer/id #uuid "ad644440-f651-5dad-b438-815e63a116ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,- \\frac{29}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509317}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509282} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bccdb9c-e6cc-546c-bc1f-af909a73f4f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ef7f3552-0ad8-5545-8673-2b2894d40ad4" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+6y&=-33\\\\2x-3y&=21\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $y$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $6$, while in the second equation it is $-3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $2$, then the $y$-coefficient will become $-6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $6$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{ -x+6y=-33; \\left(2x-3y=21\\right)\\cdot (2)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x+6y&=-33 \\\\\n4x-6y&=42 \\\\\n(-x+4x)&=(-33+42) \\\\\n3x&=9 \\\\\nx&=3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x = 3$. However, we still need to find $y$. To do this, we substitute $x = 3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x-3y&=21 \\\\\n2(3)-3y&=21 \\\\\n6-3y&=21 \\\\\n-3y&=15 \\\\\ny&=-5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is\n\n$$\nx = 3, \\,y = -5\n$$\n\nwhich can be expressed as $(3,-5)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509344 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28d9b9f6-af1e-5d04-81f6-d3e14d15ba37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{33}{5},- \\frac{166}{15})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509274} {:answer/id #uuid "4dee1735-757a-5a7e-8abc-3d08ac98a01a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{19}{33},\\frac{562}{99})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509284} {:answer/id #uuid "581c1cfe-6f4b-5f91-ad28-ceabe0e592f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509290} {:answer/id #uuid "61a29bde-d4a9-528b-90d5-e13febae164b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509294} {:answer/id #uuid "b681415e-0e9c-5a64-970d-72037254e2cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,\\frac{20}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509321}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509290} :answer-field/id #uuid "8275be3d-f06e-52aa-9799-9ef432738ad0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509305}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fe868340-7a35-5fed-a08d-ce25cbc1fbb9" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+15y&=32\\\\-7x-3y&=-13\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $y$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $y$-coefficient in the first equation is $15$, while in the second equation it is $-3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $5$, then the $y$-coefficient will become $-15$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $15$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{ 2x+15y=32; \\left(-7x-3y=-13\\right)\\cdot (5)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x+15y&=32 \\\\\n-35x-15y&=-65 \\\\\n(2x-35x)&=(32-65) \\\\\n-33x&=-33 \\\\\nx&=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x = 1$. However, we still need to find $y$. To do this, we substitute $x = 1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-7x-3y&=-13 \\\\\n-7(1)-3y&=-13 \\\\\n-7-3y&=-13 \\\\\n-3y&=-6 \\\\\ny&=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is\n\n$$\nx = 1, \\,y = 2\n$$\n\nwhich can be expressed as $(1,2)$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations by Eliminating the Second Variable"}] :topic/math-academy-id 4026 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048756} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048841} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048982} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049777} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049946}] :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}
